# k31rel. The first serving sitting of the Kimi K3.1 Pro IQ1_S set (v1: chat-rendered imatrix, bloomery-quantize), 580 GB over 31
# shards, through bloomery-serve at the serving defaults on the box alone, --place bp (RTX A6000 + RTX 3090): the set is
# larger than the host (251 GB), so the expert tier spills to nvme0 (the O_DIRECT tier) and the step is NVMe-bound.
kind: baseline
question: what decode and prompt rate does the K3.1 v1 set reach at --place bp on the box alone, D=512 and D=1536 at --ctx-size 2048, through bloomery-serve
term: decode tok/s at D=512, bloomery-serve from ~/repo/bloomery-k31rel (the tree's binary), --place bp, --ctx-size 2048, 2 rounds
unit: tok/s
predict: 0.8..3.0
condition: tools/ref/depth-serve.sh arms D=512 and D=1536 (bloomery-k31rel:512 bloomery-k31rel:1536), DEPTH_SERVE_PLACE=bp, DEPTH_SERVE_CTX=2048 (the
  K3.1 reader holds the context to the indexer's top_k, 2048: the selected attention is not in this engine, so past it the latent
  attention would read every position and the file's own context, 391168, is refused by name), the kimi-k3
  profile with BLOOMERY_REF_MODEL the v1 set's first shard on /models (nvme0), the prose corpus ids of kimi-k3, one lease, the cards
  idle at the baseline read; the first row after a cold load is marked [cold] and not read; BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=252G on
  every arm (the live MemAvailable reading moved the host expert bytes by ~0.6 GB between loads, so the rows were not one key)
reason: [derived] per token the routed experts active read ~25e9 weights at IQ1_S (0.195 B/weight) ~ 4.9 GB; the host holds ~230 GB of the
  ~515 GB of experts, the cards ~65 GB and nvme0 the rest (~220 GB, 43 %): ~2.1 GB/token from nvme0 at the measured 5.0 GB/s (the
  11-07 copy test) = 0.42 s, ~2.1 GB from host DRAM at ~40 GB/s = 0.05 s, the cards' part and the attention under them, so
  ~0.5 s/token = 2 tok/s with the NVMe term dominant; the band's low end is the NVMe at random 4 KiB..1 MiB reads (half the
  sequential rate), the high end a warmer residency than the even split. The prompt pass (k3fill, rows 256) streams the same
  experts once per 256 rows: the v1 scoring's pass over 35,226 positions in ~5,400 s read 6.5 tok/s with a load per prompt, so
  pp512 is expected at 5..15 tok/s
decide-in: write the rows into the release notes' Kimi K3.1 table with these conditions (the box alone); the Spark tier cell is a
  second sitting with its own card
decide-below: under 0.8: read the plan line (host room, nvme bytes) and the witness block (nvme0 state, the 3090's Xid lines) before
  writing a number; a tier that fell to the HDD or a card that fell off the bus is a fault, not a rate
decide-above: beyond 3.0: read the plan line (more host residency than derived) before crediting
# outcome 2026-11-07 try7 (DEPTH_SERVE_FOLD=depths, BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=252G, DEPTH_SERVE_REQ_BOUND=1800, 2 rounds): decode 3.30 / 3.32 tok/s @ D=512
#  and 2.42 / 2.42 @ D=1536; pp 2.71 / 2.84 @ D=512 and 2.70 / 2.66 @ D=1536; every row [cold] (1.2M..4.0M major faults a request, the
#  [shared] rows too: the set is larger than the host, so each request pages its experts and no request warms the next; the
#  rows repeat within 5 %, so the cold reading is this set's steady state on this box). Decode above the band's 3.0: the host
#  held 249 GB of experts (derived 230) and the page cache served part of the NVMe share. pp far under the derived 5..15: the
#  kimik3 serve seat steps the prompt one id at a time (Family::PREFILL_STEPS); the 256-row pass is generate_kimi_k3 --walk pass
#  only, not the server's, so pp ≈ tg. Earlier tries: try4 the user-plan check (the live host room moves the plan by ~0.6 GB
#  between loads), try5 plan drift for the same reason (→ the pinned room), try6 the 300 s request bound at D=1536.
# outcome 2026-11-07 @portable (the 0.3.13 sm86 tarball's bloomery-serve, sha e3dd7df6…, HOST_ROOM=252G, fold depths, 2 rounds, rc 0):
#  D=512 tg 3.04 / 3.05, pp 2.62 / 2.67; D=1536 tg 2.27 / 2.34, pp 2.58 / 2.53 (r1 / r2); load 57-58 s; every row [cold]
#  (1.4-4.4 M major faults); within 2 % between rounds, 5-8 % under the tree rows of try7 (cold scatter). The release's rows.
